hardware notes:

Ubertooth One schematic and layout files were designed in KiCad, an open source
electronic design automation package. Board makers build Ubertooth One hardware
from these files.

	ubertooth-one.sch	schematic
	ubertooth-one.brd	board layout

Both are in the file format KiCad used in 2011.

The board carries an LPC1754 or an LPC1756 depending on the build. The
schematic calls for an LPC1754, with 128 KB of flash; boards in the field are a
mix, and the LPC1756, with 256 KB, is the other part they are built with. The
bootloader reads the part identification number and sizes flash from it, so the
same firmware image serves either. Both parts have 32 KB of RAM in two 16 KB
banks that are not contiguous: the main SRAM at 0x10000000, which the firmware
runs from, and the AHB SRAM at 0x2007C000.

docs/source/ubertooth_one.rst describes the board for a user: its radio, its
connectors and its LEDs.

order of copper layers:
	Front
	Inner3
	Inner2
	Back

PCB description: 4 layer PCB 1.6 mm
	Copper        1   35 um
	Dielectric  1-2   0.35 mm
	Copper        2   18 um
	Dielectric  2-3   0.76 mm
	Copper        3   18 um
	Dielectric  3-4   0.35 mm
	Copper        4   35 um
DE104iML or equivalent substrate (Er=4.42@2.4GHz TanD=0.016)
double side solder mask black
double side silkscreen white
6 mil min trace width and
6 mil min isolation
